    {
      "title": "4 Gore Hat",
      "slug": "4-gore-hat",
      "displayOrder": 1,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 856,
        "lessonOrder": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<b>Looking for a hat pattern that actually fits well?</b><br>This 4 gore design is your answer! The shaped sections eliminate that annoying bulk at the crown while creating a more tailored look. <br>It's the perfect project to level up your machine knitting skills while making something truly useful.<br>Whether you're knitting for charity or making gifts, this pattern works beautifully with any yarn and lets you get creative with stitch patterns and colors. <br>Once you try this construction method, you'll never look back!\r\n\r\nMaster gore shaping techniques that create a better-fitting hat\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Explore methods for adding ribbing, no matter what machine you are using</li>\r\n\r\n<li>Scrapping off for knitting separate sections (gores)</li>\r\n<li>Gore shaping using decrease techniques</li>\r\n<li>Following decrease instructions</li>\r\n<li>Neat Seaming</li>\r\n<lI>Finishing</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 9899,
              "order": 1
            }
          ],
          "title": "Introduction",
          "slug": "introduction",
          "order": 1,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 6417,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
