      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<style>\r\n    .handwriting {'Handlee', cursive;\r\n        color: #9E2065;\r\n        font-weight: 600;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    .container-border1 {\r\n        border: 2px solid #ccc;\r\n        border-radius: 15px 50px;\r\n        padding-top: 20px;\r\n        padding-right: 20px;\r\n        padding-bottom: 20px;\r\n        padding-left: 20px;\r\n        background-color: white;\r\n        max-width: 700px;\r\n        margin: auto;\r\n        background-color: #DCDCDC;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    .img1 {\r\n        border: 3px solid #ccc;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n    \r\n        \r\n\r\n            <span class=\"handwriting\" style=\"font-size:2em\">Make sure it stays on!</span><br>When knitting sweaters, we add \"ease\" so the sweater doesn't cling.<br>For hats, it's important to make them smaller and incorporate <a data-GlossaryId=\"715\" class=\"glossaryhelp\">Negative Ease <i class=\"fa fa-question-circle-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></a>.<br>\r\n            <span class=\"yellow_highlight\"> By making the circumference of a hat smaller than the head size, we rely on the stretch of knitting to keep the hat on the head in the strongest wind.</span><br><b>The Knit it Now Hat sizing chart</b> helps you select your hat size and lists the head (actual) measurements.<br>\r\n            You can further adjust the FINISHED circumference when you build your custom pattern.<br><div class=\"container-border1 text-center\"><span style=\"font-size:1.25em\">Negative ease =  Body measurement <b>minus</b> Finished Measurement </span></div>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n        \r\n\r\n        <figure><img class=\"img1\" alt=\"\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/129/measure.jpg\"><br><em><figcaption align=\"center\">Don't forget NEGATIVE EASE</em></figcaption>\r\n</figure><br>\r\n    <br>\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 9962,
              "order": 1
            }
          ],
          "title": "Get the fit just right",
          "slug": "get-the-fit-just-right",
          "order": 1,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 6437,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<style>\r\n    .handwriting {'Handlee', cursive;\r\n        color: #9E2065;\r\n        font-weight: 600;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    .container-border1 {\r\n        border: 2px solid #ccc;\r\n        border-radius: 15px 50px;\r\n        padding-top: 20px;\r\n        padding-right: 20px;\r\n        padding-bottom: 20px;\r\n        padding-left: 20px;\r\n        background-color: white;\r\n        max-width: 700px;\r\n        margin: auto;\r\n        background-color: #DCDCDC;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    .img1 {\r\n        border: 3px solid #ccc;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n\r\n  \r\n\r\n<hr class=\"style13\">\r\n\r\nWith this hat,  you have complete control over the size you will knit.<br>Choose a size below and check all 3 measurements.<br><ol>\r\n<li>Choose a size below</li>\r\n<li>Click the button \"Customize your Pattern\"</li>\r\n<li>Double Check your measurements</li>\r\n<li>Enter YOUR gauge</li>\r\n<li>Click the button to \"Create Your custom pattern</li>\r\n\r\n</ol>\r\n<br>\r\nNOTE: Enter the FINAL Ribbing depth you want when wearing the hat. The pattern will instruct you to knit the ribbing section twice as long as this measurement, since it will be folded in half when worn.<br><a class=\"videopopup\" data-videotitle=\"KIN_Pattern_overview\" data-vimeoid=\"772256112\"><i class=\"fa fa-youtube-play\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Are you new to Knit it Now Patterns?\"</a>\r\n\r\n\r\n<hr class=\"style13\">",
