    {
      "title": "Wedges (Gores)",
      "slug": "wedges-gores",
      "displayOrder": 6,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 864,
        "lessonOrder": 6
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "Each wedge is shaped separately, then neatly seamed to form the top of the hat. <br><i class=\"fa fa-youtube-play\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Scrap off each section<br><blockquote style=\"background-color: #f8f9fa; padding: 15px; border-left: 5px solid #ccc; font-style: italic;\">\r\n  NOTE: To eliminate counting stitches, the pattern suggests scrapping off each wedge separately.  If you prefer, scrap off all the stitches for 3 wedges, keeping the stitches for the first wedge in work (next to the carriage). <br>\r\nAfter the first wedge has been completed, pick up another set of stitches for the next wedge and knit the 2nd wedge. Continue for all 4 wedges\r\n</blockquote>\r\n\r\n\r\n<br><button data-Machine_Tax_id='3' class='technique btn btn-primary'>Need help? Setting your machine to HOLD</button>",
              "legacyComponentId": 9948,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "1037066197",
              "title": null,
              "legacyComponentId": 9957,
              "order": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "migrationPending",
              "legacyType": "Patternshowinline",
              "notes": [
                "Unmapped legacy component type: Patternshowinline"
              ],
              "legacyFields": {
